Excellent. Now we’re moving from “How deployment works” to “Why each line in my Dockerfile exists.”

The biggest mistake beginners make is thinking:

Dockerfile = random commands that somehow make deployment work.

Actually every line is solving a specific problem.

⸻

First Let’s Remember The Goal

When Azure Container Instance does:

Download Image
Create Container
Start Container

it needs an image that contains:

Operating System
Python
Libraries
Your Code
Startup Command

Your Dockerfile defines exactly how that image should be built.

⸻

Agent Dockerfile

FROM python:3.11.5-bookworm


⸻

What does this do?

Starts with an existing image.

Think:

You are not building a house from sand.

You start with an already built house.

The image already contains:

Linux OS
Python 3.11.5
Python Runtime


⸻

Why do we need it?

Without it:

No OS
No Python
No pip

Your application cannot run.

⸻

Significance

This is the foundation of the entire image.

Think:

FROM
=
Choose the base computer


⸻

WORKDIR

WORKDIR /EmailIntentAgent


⸻

What does this do?

Creates and switches into:

/EmailIntentAgent

inside the container.

⸻

Why?

Imagine:

COPY requirements.txt .

Docker asks:

Copy where?

WORKDIR provides the answer.

⸻

Significance

Sets the default folder.

Think:

cd EmailIntentAgent

in Linux.

⸻

COPY requirements.txt .

COPY requirements.txt .


⸻

What happens?

Copies:

requirements.txt

from your laptop into:

/EmailIntentAgent

inside image.

⸻

Why?

Because next step installs packages.

Without file:

pip install -r requirements.txt

fails.

⸻

Significance

Makes dependency list available.

⸻

RUN pip install

RUN pip3 install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt


⸻

What happens?

Installs:

FastAPI
LangChain
OpenAI SDK
Azure SDK
etc.

into image.

⸻

Why?

Azure Container Instance doesn’t have these installed.

Your laptop may have:

fastapi
langchain
openai

but Azure starts from a fresh environment.

⸻

Significance

Makes image self-contained.

This is why:

Works On My Machine

becomes:

Works Anywhere


⸻

COPY . .

COPY . .


